WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.501
-You have so much to talk about,
so much coming out.

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:04.637
The new film called "The Nest,"

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:07.373
which was
a Sundance selection --

00:00:07.373 --> 00:00:08.841
it's in select theaters Friday,

00:00:08.841 --> 00:00:11.210
on demand
starting November 17th.

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.947
What -- Can you set up the film
"The Nest"?

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:17.684
-This is a film
regarding a young couple

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:21.554
who decide to leave the States
and head to London in 1986,

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.724
around the time
of the economic boom.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.359
And, really, it's just a study

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:31.164
of how a family are pulling
in different directions,

00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:32.631
all trying to keep
the family together,

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:34.000
all trying to make
the family work,

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.434
but sort of tempted,
if you like,

00:00:35.434 --> 00:00:38.705
by the lure of greed, of money,

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:42.108
and -- and not necessarily
what's best for them.

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:47.580
It's a really subtle, elegant,
beautiful look at family life.

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.982
And I had a great time
making it.

00:00:49.982 --> 00:00:53.519
Carrie Coon plays my wife,
and as I said,

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:57.057
Sean Durkin directs
really wonderfully.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:00:59.291
-This new HBO series,
limited series

00:00:59.291 --> 00:01:00.960
called "The Third Day."
-Yes.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:03.262
-I don't know how to set it up
without spoiling it.

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.565
-Okay, so there
are two sections.

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.100
The first three
are called "Summer,"

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.405
and it's about a man dealing
with terrible loss and grief.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:14.007
I don't think I'm giving
anything away by telling you

00:01:14.007 --> 00:01:16.975
he's lost his son.

00:01:16.975 --> 00:01:20.380
And he's trying to sort of heal
and remedy his life.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.682
He gets taken to an island
by a young girl

00:01:22.682 --> 00:01:24.817
who is trying to do
a good deed for --

00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.285
and gets stuck on this island.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:28.288
Now, it's an island,
a real island

00:01:28.288 --> 00:01:30.056
off the coast of Essex
called "Osea,"

00:01:30.056 --> 00:01:32.091
which has this
old Roman causeway,

00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:35.962
so it only opens, this causeway
at certain times of the day.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:38.264
And we filmed on this island.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:40.600
The community on the island
and the culture of the island

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:42.101
has been sort of elaborated,

00:01:42.101 --> 00:01:46.338
but it's really a sort of symbol
of him trying to lose the --

00:01:46.338 --> 00:01:48.507
him trying escape the isolation
of his own grief,

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.643
which is, if you like,
the metaphor for the island

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:54.480
and trying to get off this
and away from this community.

00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.849
And then the second half,
the other three,

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:58.517
are called "Winter,"

00:01:58.517 --> 00:02:01.087
and they're another perspective
of the island in the community

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:03.956
from a woman's point of view,
Naomie Harris.

00:02:03.956 --> 00:02:07.260
Now, in the middle
is a live event that links them.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:10.296
I was originally pitched this
by Felix Barrett,

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.498
who is the artistic director
of Punchdrunk,

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:15.901
who have a wonderful production
in New York

00:02:15.901 --> 00:02:17.170
and around the world.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:19.705
They were kind of creators
of immersive theater.

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:21.273
And he had this idea --
-Oh, yeah, what did --

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:22.575
what did they do?

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:23.776
-"Sleep No More."
-"Sleep No More."

00:02:23.776 --> 00:02:25.712
Yeah. Yeah, yeah, of course.
-That's right.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:27.747
So he came to me -- he had
this idea that he wanted to do,

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:31.550
like, a film story,
whether it was on TV or film,

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.586
and then a live event
that was somehow linked

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.321
to blur those lines of like,

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:36.822
"is this real?
Is this not real?

00:02:36.822 --> 00:02:38.857
Is what I'm watching
actually happening?"

00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:40.627
We're gonna have
a single camera.

00:02:40.627 --> 00:02:42.361
We'll be there as actors,
as performers,

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:44.063
and the camera will follow us

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:46.499
and the events
for 12 hours live.

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.367
So it'll be a kind of
combination

00:02:48.367 --> 00:02:52.638
of a sort of live event,
a live piece of theater,

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:56.508
a film in the --
but a film done in one take,

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:59.879
and at times, you know,
you may be watching people,

00:02:59.879 --> 00:03:02.481
like, doing some crazy,
like, pagan dancing.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:03.850
And there may be scenes.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.687
There will be moments when it's
a series of the cross

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:10.689
because it's sort of
a religious theme going through.

00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:12.558
There'll also be stuff
that I actually don't know,

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:13.893
because they're going to be
throwing things at me

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:16.062
left, right, and center
over 12 hours.

00:03:16.062 --> 00:03:18.597
-12 hours.
I mean, that is --

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:20.566
I love that you're doing this.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.602
I think it's gonna be fantastic.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.737
-That's October 3rd.
-Hopefully, hopefully.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.039
-Oh, yeah, no, I'm going
to catch up on "Summer"

00:03:27.039 --> 00:03:28.774
and get ready for October 3rd,
then...

00:03:28.774 --> 00:03:30.176
-Please do.
-...then for "Winter."

00:03:30.176 --> 00:03:32.211
Yeah, no, I'm --
I'm psyched, buddy.

00:03:32.211 --> 00:03:33.412
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:33.412 --> 00:03:35.648
Here the Jude Law
in "The Third Day."

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.916
Take a look.

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:40.787
-You -- You talked
of sacrifice here.

00:03:40.787 --> 00:03:42.555
-Sacrifice?

00:03:42.555 --> 00:03:44.957
Sam, that was 2,000 years ago.
-Look at this place.

00:03:44.957 --> 00:03:46.626
Is there anything [bleep]
normal here?

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:48.928
I found dead animals
all over this island.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.196
Who's doing that?

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.797
No, there were -- there were
pictures down there

00:03:51.797 --> 00:03:53.866
hanging on the wall
of Jack the Ripper's victims.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.535
Is that standard?

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:57.403
Men in masks
have just chased me.

00:03:57.403 --> 00:03:58.671
Someone nearly shot me.

00:03:58.671 --> 00:04:00.506
-Okay, if this is all true,
then what do we do?

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.175
-We get off the island!

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:04.143
We find a phone.
We call the police now.

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.744
-Okay, how?

00:04:05.744 --> 00:04:08.180
-[ Sighs ]

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.148
Can you swim?

00:04:10.148 --> 00:04:11.450
-Jude Law, everybody.

00:04:11.450 --> 00:04:14.887
Check out "The Third Day"
on HBO and HBO Max

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.455
and "The Nest"

00:04:16.455 --> 00:04:20.260
in select theaters Friday
and on demand November 17th.

00:04:20.260 --> 00:04:21.593
Thank you so much
for being here, Jude.

00:04:21.593 --> 00:04:23.095
I really, really appreciate it.

00:04:23.095 --> 00:04:25.030
-Honestly,
I will never, ever forget

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:26.765
the fact that
you've come into my house.

00:04:26.765 --> 00:04:28.034
I love it.
-Thanks for --

00:04:28.034 --> 00:04:30.736
Thanks for having me,
and kiss that baby.

00:04:30.736 --> 00:04:32.004
-I will.
-Bye, buddy.

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:34.207
-Thank you, I will.
Over and over. Best wishes.

00:04:34.207 --> 00:04:35.575
Bye, everyone.
-Thank you. Bye, bud.

